OL,3,GNEWSATouching reason teen has decided
OL,4,Ato shave his head
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 13-year-old boy is having his head
OL,7,Fshaved to raise money for a hospice
OL,8,Fwhich is supporting his mum, who has
OL,9,Fstage four cancer.
OL,11,FHenry, from Warrington, Cheshire,
OL,12,Fdecided he wanted to give back to St
OL,13,FRocco's Hospice in the town, which has
OL,14,Fbeen providing palliative care and
OL,15,Fsupport to his mum Sarah, 43, after she
OL,16,Fwas diagnosed with bowel cancer about
OL,17,F18 months ago.
OL,19,FHenry said: "She has had multiple
OL,20,Foperations which were unsuccessful and
OL,21,Fshe is now on palliative treatment to
OL,22,Fprolong her life.
OL,23,APub: 04-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
